.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3685669678">January 2, 2021</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Ruthless King is the first book in Alison Aimes’s brand new series, Ruthless Warlords. This book takes place in Anarcheim, a parallel Alphaverse galaxy in a dark future seeded with various forms of alien life. But in this world, there are two constants. All inhabitants are Alpha, beta or omega. Alphas lead, betas serve, and omegas submit. I just this minute finished this book and am staring at the computer trying to find the words to tell you how amazing this book was and the words are not coming to me. Other than to just say just that, this is an amazing book you do not want to miss.<br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608928._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Dahlia Lundin is twenty four years old and is an omega. To her father, she is simply a pawn to be given to the highest bidder. But when her father has a large debt that needs to be paid, his plans change and his daughter now becomes a way to pay his debt. When Dahlia sees who she is being given to, she comes face to face with a man she met once before as a little boy. A connection was formed that day that she has never forgotten, that has helped to get her through her darkest days. But this alpha is no little boy.<br><br><b>
  <i>“His past and her future were linked, but it seemed increasingly clear that only one of them would survive the battle coming.”</i>
</b><br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608929.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Nikolai Skolov barely survived his childhood, his soul purpose was keeping his siblings alive. Nikolai is an alpha and has amassed great wealth. The one thing besides taking care of his brothers and sister that kept him going was that he would someday take possession of the omega he met when he was a boy. He would possess her and never let her go. <br><br><b>
  <i>“She might be his pawn, but she was his salvation too.”</i>
</b><br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608930._SX540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Nikolai needs something from Dahlia, something that would make her betray her family. They may never have shown her love or compassion but they are still her family. Her alpha now owns her, but she is determined not to give him what he needs. What she hadn’t counted on is the bond that is quickly forming between them. They are very rare fated mates. The more time they spend together, the deeper the bond becomes, until it becomes impossible for her to determine where she ends and he begins. Where a hunger for the passion her alpha introduces her to becomes the center of her world. But also, where her loyalties are continuously challenged, and she discovers a strength within her she never knew existed.<br><br><b>
  <i>“He was her leader, her master, her mate, her treasure, and her love.”<br><br>“You are my beginning and my end, my wildest obsession, my greatest purpose.”</i>
</b><br><br>This book pretty much rocked my world. Alison Aimes words are pure magic. This is dark, yes. But, it’s also beautiful. The bond between these two was so powerful. It went against everything that was believed possible between an alpha and his omega. Nikolai was ruthless. He was powerful and feared. There was one tiny little omega, though, that he didn’t want to fear him, that he wanted to trust him. One tiny little omega that he would burn down the universe to keep her safe if he had to. His Dahlia.<br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608931._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>After reading this, now I’m on pins and needles to get the next book. It will focus on another of Nikolai’s siblings but I don’t know which one. It will be entitled Savage Prince.<br><br><b>
  <i>“My treasure, my mate, my queen.”</i>
