>Style: Dark Mafia Romance (Sci-Fi)<br />Story: 4/5<br />Enjoyment: 4/5<br />Dark Level: 1.5/5 <br />Sexual Level: SEX-CITINGLY GOOD<br />Triggers: No<br />Violence: Yes<br />Male: Intense, Sexy and Alpha<br />Series: book 1<br />Pages: 380<br />Audio: GOOD(m/f)<br />Kindle Unlimited: No<br /><br /><br />STORY:<br />I have read Omegaverse books, but I didn’t know what to expect from an Omegaverse Mafia Romance. I really liked this one and the blurb was eye catching as well. You have the story between Nikolai and Dahlia, and the story of what Nikolai is trying to uncover with his family and their past. This was a payment debt/mated theme, and it held true to that. Nikolai, was very Alpha in this book. Intense and at times, and soft when he needed to be, but not in a way that is off putting. Nikolai came from nothing, so his ruthlessness is born from that. Dahlia was a very likable character. She doesn’t have the best relationship with her father, however, he uses her to get what he needs. I liked that Dahlia had special powers, and it evolved as her character evolved. This was dark, but it wasn’t hardcore dark.<br /><br />I really love the male actor who does Nikolai’s voice. I think that's a big part of why I love this. He brought his character to life for me. <br /><br /><br /><br /><br />SEXUAL CHEMISTRY:<br />Sex scenes were good for my liking. In Omegaverse, I always find it appealing when betas can’t control their needs to their mated Alphas. <br /><br /><br />SECONDARY CHARACTERS:<br />Dahlia’s family, mmmmm the nicest way to describe them, crazy. However, Nikolai’s family love them. Maxheim sexy. Hopefully I get to read his story soon. <br /><br /><br /><br />OVERALL:<br />I love the characters and I really enjoyed the plot of the story. <br /><br /><br /><br />TRIGGERS: violence<br /><br /><br />****I don’t equate these stories to real life. It’s about personal taste and what you would or want to tolerate with the books you read. I know we all have different