75 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-1small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-1small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8211569742">January 5, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Sci-fi ish mafia omegaverse with mystery and a bit of fantasy too.<br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1767612780i/37439756._SX540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br><b>Plot</b><br><br>Dahlia Lundin is an omega "sold" to Nikolai Skolov by her father as a debt payment. Lundins and Skolovs are both powerful mafia families and are feuding with one another. We figured out during the "payment meeting" that Dahlia and Nikolai are fated mates. Dahlia was hopeful with her new match, hoping Nikolai is the same boy she met long ago. Nikolai wanted her since the first time they met, but he also needed her to use her omega gift to save his family.<br><br><br><b>Review</b><br><br>I thought I would like this more. I genuinely just read this for the omegaverse part, but was hit by a ton of... magic, sci-fi, mystery, politics. It's very plot heavy, though the smut is delicious, and romance is definitely there. I do have a bit of complaints though.<br><br>First, the hero. I seriously don't get the guy. He knows Dahlia was being treated poorly by her family, and he wants her taken care of, yet he's doing everything but communicating. He spanks her and put her in some kind of fridge to the point she wanted to kill herself. ALL AVOIDABLE btw with a bit of communicating.<br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1767612780i/37439757._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>It also is just a bit of a contradiction. If we only see him from her perspective it would have made sense why he was being so rough. He didn't love her yet. But him, in his pov, being like "oh i want her, i want to take care of her" and then proceeding to threaten her and refuse to offer help or give clear communication is just??? weird!!!<br><br>Also weird: He was being so forceful because he was trying to awaken her magic so he could save his family and solve mystery. The times Dahlia's magic are strongest was when they were fucking and they were happy. And then he proceed to be rough and threaten her?? Nikolai had to be TOLD by a fucking DOCTOR who had to STUDY a book to figure out he had to be nice to her.<br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1767612780i/37439758._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Excuse moi??? I thought it was fucking obvious?? Need magic=magic when happy=don't threaten 👉 make omega happy, get magic.<br><br>Does it really take a group of men in a council meeting and a doctor doing research to figure out that in order to get the magic an omega needs to be happy?? One woman would have solved it in a second. Or you know, you would've figured it out yourself if you were just a DECENT man.<br><br>Then after knowing that they're like "Well, we're fucked". I don't know guys, why don't we just... communicate???<br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1605640702ra/30390914.gif" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>No wonder they can't solve the mystery for fifteen fucking years. Also speaking of the mystery, it is all so very obvious who did the murdering and everything. You could see it a mile away.<br><br>As for the omega, Dahlia. I'm also annoyed at her at one point. She refused to help Skolovs and communicate too, even though she knew her family was bad and guilty. She says, "I won't betray my family, my sister". I don't know, why don't you make a deal with the Skolovs to spare the innocents instead of refusing to help justice altogether? Seems a bit weird. <br><br>Her denial gets tiring after a while too. While her sister was saved so she has no other reason to not help the Skolovs, she kept saying "oh but my mother" and "oh i can't betray my family". GIRL??? The mother who told you to kill yourself? The family that sold you and mistreated you?? Get a grip. <br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1767612780ra/37439759.gif" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>There is some good bit though. There's a reason this is all fantasy. The man apologised. Yeah, you heard that right. An alpha man in omegaverse says "I'm sorry."<br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1767612780ra/37439760.gif" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>It became better after that part honestly, though the author went back and forth with making him good and then an ass and then good again.<br><br>Also why is he called "King"? The mafia Brotherhood seemed more like a council to me. Calling himself king should be like... weird and out of place, yk. <br><br>As for the good stuff. Romance part is good I guess. Hero was sweet toward the end and lost his earlier personality. The whole "fated mate" works well, I just wished we see more of their personality outside the plot. For the smut, it was hot, and there's smut throughout, but the plot is heavier toward the end with less and less smut.<br><br><b>Conclusion</b><br><br>I feel like the first half doesn't have good romance but has good smut, and the second half has good romance and less good smut. Plot on murderers and mystery are infuriating for me because they just went about it all wrong, and wasted so much time. But they did get there eventually. Characters are infuriating at times but it works.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/86342358?shelf=nastay" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">nastay</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/86342358?shelf=omegaverse" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">omegaverse</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">10 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19