981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3804325017">January 29, 2021</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">4.75 Smutty Omegaverse Light Stars!<br /><br />This is the first book in Aimes' Mafia Omegaverse series and I really loved this story about Nikolai and Dahlia. I'm always hesitant to pick up an Omegaverse because some are entirely too dark for me. But I would classify this as light with just the right amount of heat.<br /><br />Nikolai and Dahlia meet at a young age and recognize what they are to each other - fated mates. However, due to the circumstances of their families and their age, they part ways but not before Nikolai says he will be back for her one day. <br /><br />Several years later, Dahlia has suffered and grown up feeling like a pawn within the world her father is a part of and with no control over her future. She despises her omega nature and wants to be free. Free to make her own choices and save her sister the fate of also being a pawn. It quickly becomes clear to Dahlia that her father owes money to Nikolai (who has risen high in power) and ends up as payment for his debts, becoming the property of Nikolai. There is a long standing fued between Nikolai and her father and he plans to have and keep her, as well as use her gift (the sight) to bring justice to his family. <br /><br />However, Nikolai quickly realizes that having a fated mate proves to be much different than he was expecting and their relationship can either make their bond strong and resilient or crumble and ruin them. It's evident to both of them that their fated mate bond can be a strength in their fight against Dahlia's father and their quest to find out who is behind some nefarious actions should they choose to nurture it. But the matter of trusting one another is more difficult than either one of them expected.<br /><br />Without giving too much away, the suspense and action revolving around their budding relationship is exciting and very well written. I was only annoyed a few times at Nikolai for being so stubborn which is where my rating came from. I was on the edge of my seat waiting to see what would happen and I truly enjoyed the twists and turns. <br /><br />Dahlia was such a great heroine. I loved that she was strong in her own way and really shined by the end. She was kind, loyal, compassionate, persevering and tender-hearted. I also loved Nikolai's siblings and I'm interested in their stories. <br /><br />What I loved most about Nikolai is that he recognized Dahlia's worth and strived to make her see that as well. Nikolai taught her that the lioness does not try to be the lion. A lioness embraces her role as the lioness. He helps her to see that she is powerful and strong and should never mistake her meekness for weakness. He was such a typical alpha but so swoon worthy. I loved his controlling and possessive nature and his almost teddy bear change in character with Dahlia. <br /><br />Overall, a great read with a wonderful ending that left me smiling and rooting for this couple.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">9 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">5 comments</span></button></div></div><di