16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-1small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-1small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7060613037">December 6, 2024</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Another one I read well before the holiday, so this isn’t the freshest. It’s a unique/odd world that wasn’t totally fleshed out, but it sounded like there are different alien species (maybe) that form some sort of mobster committee of crime lords. I’m not sure if they’re all alphas, but many of them are and they have stables of Omegas with a Prime Omega that (I think) he has his kids with. As common in most Omegaverse reads, the alphas are on top with all the power and the omegas are on the bottom and largely controlled by their body responses. She will eventually “tame” her alpha, but it takes a while. So, FYI if that isn’t you’re thing.<br /><br />Nikolai met Dahlia when they were kids when he was in a desperate situation with his siblings. The two knew they had a connection, and he vowed to return for her. The book opens many years later with him fulfilling that pledge. Within the first few chapters, we learn <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="c45d9a18-8440-4659-be35-9ffc4a9113c4" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="c45d9a18-8440-4659-be35-9ffc4a9113c4"> they are fated mates</label> which is very rare, but not surprising with what we had been told and shown up to that point.<br /><br />The rest is a lot of smut and some tension because Nikolai wants Dahlia to use her Omega gift to help him finally get his revenge on her abusive, murdering father which she is resistant to. At first this made sense because she was trying to protect her sister, but I started to lose patience with her after he resolved that for her, and she still continued to be obstinate. <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="bc7e583c-102b-4a7c-9d48-125271cf2b25" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="bc7e583c-102b-4a7c-9d48-125271cf2b25"> Add in her decision at the end to let the murdering villain escape who had just tried to kill her bond mate and tried to kill then kidnap her <b>AND</b> wouldn’t hesitate to do so again, and I lost ALL respect for Dum-Dum Dahlia.</label><br /><br />My biggest grump was how long the push pull went on. I prefer it when my H and h work as a team against the baddies rather than battling each other, and this dynamic started to drag at times. Dahlia waffling for her abusive family that has treated her like crap and Nikolai being an ass because he’s pissed that she’s prioritizing her terrible family. On and on… blah blah blah. With loads of BBS and sex.<br /><br /><u>Bottom Line</u>- I liked it, but I didn’t love it. I thought it ran too long for a book heavily smut based, and Dahlia REALLY pushed my patience with her dumb devotion to assholes. I thought the twist was fairly obvious and guessed correctly mid-book.<br /><br />It looks like the next book will follow the same formula, another omega that is torn between her fated mate that has 100% been wronged by her evil family or friends (in this case murdered H’s mother and kidnaped his siblings) and her waffling between loyalties… no thanks.<br /><br /><u>Safety</u>- <i> Unlike most of the Alpha crime heads, he had no stable of omegas, indentured or otherwise, and no long line of official offspring or bastards, either. At age twenty-eight, that was almost unheard of. He fucked when he needed release, but until now he’d never had an omega of his own. He’d known, after meeting her, no one else would do.</i><br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/80698268?shelf=omegaverse" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">omegaverse</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/80698268?shelf=smut" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">smut</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">8 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444