Goodreads Addict]","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/10717098-carol-goodreads-addict","contributor":null,"id":10717098},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/10717098?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3685669678"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.g7USq4SDEHzaBmSpFE8SqA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.g7USq4SDEHzaBmSpFE8SqA","creator":{"__ref":"User:10717098"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1697433811058,"createdAt":1609292374165,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1609590881865,"text":"Ruthless King is the first book in Alison Aimes’s brand new series, Ruthless Warlords. This book takes place in Anarcheim, a parallel Alphaverse galaxy in a dark future seeded with various forms of alien life. But in this world, there are two constants. All inhabitants are Alpha, beta or omega. Alphas lead, betas serve, and omegas submit. I just this minute finished this book and am staring at the computer trying to find the words to tell you how amazing this book was and the words are not coming to me. Other than to just say just that, this is an amazing book you do not want to miss.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608928._SY540_.jpg\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDahlia Lundin is twenty four years old and is an omega. To her father, she is simply a pawn to be given to the highest bidder. But when her father has a large debt that needs to be paid, his plans change and his daughter now becomes a way to pay his debt. When Dahlia sees who she is being given to, she comes face to face with a man she met once before as a little boy. A connection was formed that day that she has never forgotten, that has helped to get her through her darkest days. But this alpha is no little boy.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“His past and her future were linked, but it seemed increasingly clear that only one of them would survive the battle coming.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608929.jpg\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNikolai Skolov barely survived his childhood, his soul purpose was keeping his siblings alive. Nikolai is an alpha and has amassed great wealth. The one thing besides taking care of his brothers and sister that kept him going was that he would someday take possession of the omega he met when he was a boy. He would possess her and never let her go. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“She might be his pawn, but she was his salvation too.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608930._SX540_.jpg\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNikolai needs something from Dahlia, something that would make her betray her family. They may never have shown her love or compassion but they are still her family. Her alpha now owns her, but she is determined not to give him what he needs. What she hadn’t counted on is the bond that is quickly forming between them. They are very rare fated mates. The more time they spend together, the deeper the bond becomes, until it becomes impossible for her to determine where she ends and he begins. Where a hunger for the passion her alpha introduces her to becomes the center of her world. But also, where her loyalties are continuously challenged, and she discovers a strength within her she never knew existed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“He was her leader, her master, her mate, her treasure, and her love.”\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e“You are my beginning and my end, my wildest obsession, my greatest purpose.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis book pretty much rocked my world. Alison Aimes words are pure magic. This is dark, yes. But, it’s also beautiful. The bond between these two was so powerful. It went against everything that was believed possible between an alpha and his omega. Nikolai was ruthless. He was powerful and feared. There was one tiny little omega, though, that he didn’t want to fear him, that he wanted to trust him. One tiny little omega that he would burn down the universe to keep her safe if he had to. His Dahlia.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1609292383i/30608931._SY540_.jpg\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter reading this, now I’m on pins and needles to get the next book. It will focus on another of Nikolai’s siblings but I don’t know which one. It will be entitled Savage Prince.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“My treasure, my mate, my queen.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor more about this book and so many others, come and visit me at Carol's Crazy Bookish World.\u003cbr\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/CarolsCrazyBookishWorld\"\u003ehttps://www.facebook.com/groups/Carol...\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1502304251i/23548582.jpg\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1HX9RKZVGY6BW\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2\"}}"},"likeCount":76,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":7},"User:11626803":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":11626803,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1700448182i/11626803._UX200_CR0,29,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":36791,"textReviewsCount":2155,"name":"Val ⚓️ Shameless Handmaiden ⚓️","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/11626803-val-shameless-handmaiden","contributor":null,"id":11626803},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11626803?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"3-stars","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11626803?shelf=3-stars"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"alphas-omegas-or-omegaverse","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11626803?shelf=alphas-omegas-or-omegaverse"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"smut-scale","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11626803?shelf=smut-scale"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3890578802"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.M9c9ANder3qiP3Xzjy64wQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.M9c9ANder3qiP3Xzjy64wQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:11626803"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1755221542774,"createdAt":1615795010296,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1615896086889,"text":"\u003cb\u003e3.5 Stars\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI liked this, but for some reason I thought I would like it more...I have a feeling I will like it more after another re-read. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eStill, a super solid omegaverse and I look forward to the next one in the series. ","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ABSF31D7FMC7V\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF\"}}"},"likeCount":98,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:81374210":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":81374210,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1741829273i/81374210._UX200_CR0,39,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":623,"textReviewsCount":808,"name":"Meredith is a hot mess","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/81374210-meredith-is-a-hot-mess","contributor":null,"id":81374210},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1N803JX1NEO91":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1N803JX1NEO91"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1N803JX1NEO91\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1N803JX1NEO91","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1N803JX1NEO91"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.-O-J7qJbFw-gisg2"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"omegaverse","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=omegaverse"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"aliens","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=aliens"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"mafia","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=mafia"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"omegaverse-dark","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=omegaverse-dark"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"faves-omegaverse","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=faves-omegaverse"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"revenge","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=revenge"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"sibling-love","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=sibling-love"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"tearjerker","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=tearjerker"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3740378266"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Jmz25Geveyp9TWPx31aybg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Jmz25Geveyp9TWPx31aybg","creator":{"__ref":"User:81374210"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1773942780432,"createdAt":1610474451666,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1648779415785,"text":"\u003cb\u003eEdit:\u003c/b\u003e 4 stars is my honest rating, but my more technical rating is 3.75 stars, because this book was too long. I'm being brutally honest with myself and my ratings and going back reevaluating them. I initially rated other books in this series 4 stars, but in all honesty they were more a 3 star read for me because of the length. A valid criticism is these books are too long. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI am left stunned. Alison Aimes' writing is fast-paced, energetic, and vibrant. With her debut Omegaverse book she's already established herself as a top tier Omegaverse author. For those familiar with her Condemned series this won't come as a surprise, but for Omegaverse readers new to Alison Aimes you're going to want to check this one out. The alien/sci fi element is strong--for sci fi romance lovers who may not be attracted to mafia, don't let the mafia element scare you away from the story. I thought the combination was fab. This is basically mafia in outer space. This book is a \u003cb\u003estandalone that ends with a satisfying HEA\u003c/b\u003e :) \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAimes is a new to me author, I requested an ARC when I noticed Ruthless King up for pre-order on Amazon based on the cover and word mafia alone. I was a bit worried the book wouldn't deliver on the promises in the blurb, but there was no need to worry - this book delivers. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e✦ \u003cb\u003eThe setting\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1610471855i/30685635.jpg\" width=\"500\" height=\"480\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eAnarcheim, a parallel Alphaverse galaxy in a dark future seeded with varied forms of alien life. There are, however, two immutable constants. The first is that all inhabitants are Alpha, beta, or omega. Alphas lead, betas serve, and omegas submit. That is the way. The second is that violence is a way of life, power is essential to survival, and crime is king.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe author did an amazing job of setting up her Omegaverse world, and it's clear enough that I can wholly recommend it to those new to Omegaverse. If you like sci fi romance, but haven't tried Omegaverse yet, this book would be a great place to start. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe author's descriptions of the various planets and areas within Anarcheim were stunning. I noticed this after reading a couple books in her Condemned series, but she has a way of bringing the setting to life. Much of this book takes place on an icy planet, Abzal, and the descriptions were to die for. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e✦ \u003cb\u003eNikolai\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e“Your chance for freedom ended fifteen years ago. Your fate set the moment we met.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNikolai was swoon worthy. The type of Alpha who is an @hole but ends up caving to his Omega and doing anything to protect her. My favorite mafia aspect of this book was how loyal Nikolai treated his family. He was willing to do anything to avenge the ones he lost and protect the ones he loved. His back story was gut wrenching! Props to the author for writing *that* scene so early in book, my jaw dropped. But going back to family, in Omegaverse there is such emphasis on the Omegas' ability to breed, I'm always surprised to not see as many children or families depicted in the stories. This book depicted how important family lines are within the Brotherhood. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile I'm shelving this as dark Omegaverse, this is on the lighter side of dark. There are heavy, dark themes, but Nikolai was not a cruel Alpha like in the darkest Omegaverses. He had his moments, he was certainly an asshole at times, but there was an overarching theme of both MCs learning how to respect and trust each other. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e✦ \u003cb\u003eDahlia\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1610468912i/30685418._SY540_.jpg\" width=\"460\" height=\"450\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDahlia was snarky without crossing into bratty territory (something I always appreciate). Those who like strong heroines who push back against the Alpha will like Dahlia. Another pet peeve I have is authors writing 'strong' heroines but all they do is talk back to the hero (it's like the author thinks that's enough to advertise a 'strong heroine'). Dahlia had her own goals, took action to meet them, and came into her own power by the end of the book. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI wouldn't describe this book as enemies to lovers per se - this ended up being a childhood meet cute to separation to love story which I ate up. Both protagonists come from families with an ongoing blood feud, and Dahlia is key to how Nikolai will enact his revenge upon her family. This created an angsty push and pull between the two. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e \u003cb\u003e“I see.” “I doubt you do. This is going to get uglier before it gets better. War is coming, the full extent of the player involved still to be determined, and you’re at the center of it all.\"\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis is a standalone, but there's still a lot going on this world and I can't wait for more. It looks like each book in this series will be Nikolai's brothers being paired with their Omegas (and I'm eager for what will either be Nikolai's sister or Dahlia's sister's story!). \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eTrigger Warnings\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"fbd64d58-4940-4fa4-a8c2-6e33ea1f0e9c\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"fbd64d58-4940-4fa4-a8c2-6e33ea1f0e9c\"\u003eViolence, murder, references to childhood abuse (brief), and dubcon --\u0026gt;the forced seduction trope, the omega caves to the bond, especially in the beginning, when she doesn't want too\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSafety\u003c/b\u003e: \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"d5c1b2d7-0f01-445f-8f2b-7c6bcc14ce89\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"d5c1b2d7-0f01-445f-8f2b-7c6bcc14ce89\"\u003eNo cheating, no ow drama. Alpha is possessive and caring of his omega\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eWordcount\u003c/b\u003e: 97K! This is a \u003cu\u003elengthy\u003c/u\u003e book. So many Omegaverse books are on the shorter side, it's awesome to find a quality, full length Omegaverse story. I felt fully satiated after reading. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eThis is a standalone and ends with a HEA\u003c/b\u003e No cliffhanger :)\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNotes:\u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"33b32ffc-181a-446c-bb36-516d2392fce6\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"33b32ffc-181a-446c-bb36-516d2392fce6\"\u003eThese are just random notes for myself! please don't read if you haven't read the book!\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI liked that it was typical for the Alphas to have an 'Omega Prime' as well as 'Omega Property' kept in stables. I feel Omegaverse reverse harems are highly unrealistic, and think it's more realistic an Alpha would have a harem. No worries for those concerned about safety though! The H doesn't have Omega stables :) \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI really liked how the Omegas gift tied into the fated mate bond, emotionally and physically. How it tied into the Omega Prime status as well.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI swooned when I learned Nikolai kept the necklace! I love it when there are objects of importance like that in a story! \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI appreciated certain world build details, like how gems had their own name, I cracked up at the phrase, 'Alpha bitch,' similar to how guys don't want to be seen as 'whipped.' \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePlot twist was fab. Well constructed plot with foreshadowing, which is difficult to do. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eConstructive criticism: This is me nitpicking, nothing major at all needs to be changed. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDuring dialogue, at one point Nikolai said: “What does the fated-mate bond tell you?” @63% in the story. This is serious nitpicking, but saying the full thing, 'fated mate bond,' seemed slightly unnatural and like a mouthful. I would think it would be more natural for him to shorten it to bond. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThere were times in the story where there could have been more subtlety and nuances of a scene left to the reader to interpret, but I felt instead the nuances and implications of a scene were spelled out to the reader. This is criticism to take with a grain of salt, because I think the majority of readers like having that--but here's an example of what I'm referring too: \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e@53%: \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ci\u003eEqually bad was the memory of how, for a few heartbeats before he fucked it up, her gaze had been warm and welcoming, the golden glow flowing from her to him along the deepening fated-mate bond making him feel lighter than he had in ages—until the vision and his knee-jerk angry reaction messed everything up. He’d struck out, wanting to prove he was strong, despite what she’d seen. All he’d done was prove what an asshole he really was.\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis was a really great scene, before the reader had experienced it from Dahlia's point of view, and how she felt hated/resented by Nikolai for experiencing a vision that he wanted no one else to see. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThen the book switches to Nikolai's POV and we learn he is feeling regret for his reaction to Dahlia. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI was able to recognize Nikolai's regret pretty quickly. This nuance was explained to the reader a few times, that by the time I got to the paragraph above, it felt slightly repetitious. I think not all of it was necessary and a few sentences could have been edited out. This is very minor, me nitpicking, but something I would mention to an author if I was beta reading. Personal taste comes into play too--I like being able to read between the lines a bit and pay attention to subtext. I think there could be room for the author to balance this a little bit more. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOne more thing I liked about the world:\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHow the balance between the Brotherhood alliance was shaky and easily unbalanced. Alphas are *so* aggressive \u0026amp; territorial, that it seemed very realistic that the Brotherhood would need to take all kinds of precautions to keep the Alphas from murdering each other. All the details from the glass encasements at the meetings, to serious consequences for the Brotherhood killing other members etc was great. I also appreciated how there was variety among the Omegas personality, some scheming, some sociopaths, some nurturing/kind, they all had personalities and their own interests. \u003cbr