At":1778130520168,"text":"5 stars \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhile listening to the audiobook I went from thinking “oh, this set up is delicious” to “hmm might dnf” to “omg loved this so much”. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe set up: Dahlia (the FMC) is given to mafia crime boss Nikolai Skolov (the MMC) as payment for a debt owed by her abusive father. And even though Nikolai knows she’s his fated mate, he plans to use her as a pawn against her father. The potential for angsty and soapy drama hooked me almost immediately. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe might dnf moment: this is a dark mafia AND alien omegaverse romance… and what do those have in common? Women and omegas basically have no agency. I find it hard to read that in a romance, especially if the MMC also treats the FMC like property without her own thoughts and feelings. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe omg I loved it so much: I’m so glad I stuck with this book because Dahlia’s agency and power was dealt with in a satisfying way, and Nikolai stayed ruthless throughout the book but towards the end there was no doubt that he put her first.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLoved this so much. Can’t wait to read the next book!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e------------\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eRe-listen on 7 May 2026 - just as good as the first time! I’m glad I didn’t put a bunch of spoilers in my review, because I’d forgotten a lot of the details and could go on the journey again. What a ride. It’s also totally daddy kink coded, even if that’s never explicitly mentioned in the book. 😏","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3H5WE0UGBDIFK\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.MQ1X-qLSE3uq-oEF\"}}"},"likeCount":12,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":7},"User:6499789":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":6499789,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/17817266